1713884	<note n="1" c="&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;Kammenhuber 1986a&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;, 94 reads &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Luwian&gt;&lt;del_in/&gt;&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Luwian&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;(UZU)&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Luwian&gt;ḫa-ap-pí-ša-a-t&lt;del_fin/&gt;i&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Luwian&gt;. Yet, the traces visible on the photograph of the tablet correspond better to the end of a &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;A&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt; sign (for the plural &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;ḪÁ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;), instead of a &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;TI&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt; sign. &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;Starke 1985a&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;, 146 fn. 22 also considers the reading &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;TI&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt; very unlikely, but what he interprets as the end of a horizontal rather resembles the head of a vertical."/>
